# oracle: pair_style srp (src/MISC/pair_srp.cpp and fix_srp.cpp at b332f28, ported in src/engine-gpl/srp): examples/PACKAGES/srp/in.srp cut down to 50 steps (3000 DPD beads in chains, 2700 bonds: hybrid dpd 1.0 1.0 373692 srp 0.8 1 mid, bond particles of type 2 inserted at the bond midpoints at the setup, excluded from type 1, in no group; newton on on, comm_modify cutoff 3.6). w206sr_chain.data is examples/PACKAGES/srp/data.chain byte for byte.
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): engine vs native thermo max rel 9.6e-15, final per-atom state max rel 3.2e-12; the forces of the final dump are those native keeps per storage slot after post_run deletes the bond particles (AtomVec::copy does not move f).
# oracle-inputs: w206sr_chain.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      full
boundary p p p
special_bonds lj/coul 1 1 1
newton on on
read_data w206sr_chain.data
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 10 check yes
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      * 225.0 0.85
comm_modify vel yes
comm_modify cutoff 3.6
pair_style      hybrid dpd 1.0 1.0 373692 srp 0.8 1 mid
pair_coeff      1 1 dpd 60.0 4.5 1.0
pair_coeff      1 2 none
pair_coeff      2 2 srp 100.0
variable        natoms equal count(all)
variable        nPotEng equal c_thermo_pe/v_natoms
thermo 10
thermo_style custom step temp pe v_nPotEng press atoms v_natoms lx ly lz
thermo_modify format float %.15g
fix  1 all nve
timestep        0.01
run          50
